WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.650
Sri Lanka, 19 May 2009.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.010
The government claimed victory over
the Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam.

3
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:13.470
It ended a civil war of about
26 years, fought since 1983.

4
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.710
The Tigers had fought to establish
Tamil Eelam in the north and east.

5
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:23.130
In the 2012 census, the Northern
Province was 93.8 per cent Tamil.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.370
The war is over.

7
00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.950
But has the conflict
behind it really ended?

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.970
Or was it never really an
ethnic conflict at all?

9
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.430
In this mission, you'll trace its causes,

10
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.490
from independence in 1948
to the outbreak of war.

11
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.570
Then you'll follow a
ceasefire that failed,

12
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.110
and weigh the evidence from after 2009.

13
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.330
Your mission: judge whether Sri
Lanka's conflict has really ended,

14
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:48.670
now the war is over.
